@meta
id: 31-04
title: Drill — translate one option
chapter: 31
type: drill
skills: lua-config
par: 42
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: nothing — there is no line to type
open: init.lua

@brief
Eight times: add the Lua translation of

    set ignorecase

to the end of the file, and save. Nothing to work out. The shape
`vim.opt.<name> = true` is one you will type a few hundred times if you
switch, and it should come out of your fingers without a pause.

Graded in vim. The Lua is written, never run.

@keys
| `G` `o` | open a line at the bottom |
| `Esc` `:wq` | out and save |

@hints
`Go`, then the line, then Esc.
--
Booleans are spelled out: `= true`, never a bare `vim.opt.ignorecase`.

@solution
    G o vim.opt.ignorecase = true <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Thirty-two keystrokes. By rep eight you should not be reading the option
name off the vimrc line any more — you should be reading `set ignorecase`
and typing the Lua straight through.

Worth knowing while you drill: `vim.opt.<name>` accepts any option vim
has, including ones with awkward names. `set ts=4` is `vim.opt.tabstop = 4`
— Lua has no abbreviations, so the port is also a good excuse to write out
what the two-letter settings in your vimrc actually mean.

@start init.lua
-- Search
vim.opt.hlsearch = true
vim.opt.incsearch = true

@expected init.lua
-- Search
vim.opt.hlsearch = true
vim.opt.incsearch = true
vim.opt.ignorecase = true
